   "he": "וְרַבִּי מַתִּיר עַד שֶׁבַע. וְהָתַנְיָא: רַבִּי מַתִּיר עַד שְׁלֹשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה! נוֹטֶה שָׁאנֵי.",
   "en": "It was taught in the Tosefta: «And Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «permits up to seven.» The Gemara asks: «Wasn’t it taught» in a baraita that for a sandal with an uneven sole, «Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «permits up to thirteen?» The Gemara answers: An «uneven» sole «is different.» Since the nails are inserted for the purpose of straightening the sole, it does not have the legal status of a spiked sandal."
  }
